{"game": "risk-of-rain-2013", "language": "english", "appid": 248820, "month": "2020-03", "window": 2, "start_date": 1583625600, "end_date": 1584316799, "month_true_total": 90, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-10-07 09:17:30 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "65091397", "author": {"steamid": "76561198061119663", "personaname": "K3nny", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198061119663/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 4, "playtime_forever": 2899, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 2899, "last_played": 1570324180, "avatar": "ab9bfc864f15872642540fe4950200ea5839a031"}, "language": "english", "review": "This game is a masterpiece. I've had so much fun playing it back in the day, that when I heard the sequel was coming out I knew I had to buy it, and so I did. All of that thanks to the original.\n\nThe one thing this game has done better over the second one IMO is the soundtrack. Whenever I get to the last level and Coalescence by Chris Christodoulou starts playing, I get hyped and feel like nothing can stop me, until a jelly fish takes almost half my hp. But that's not to say RoR2 doesn't have an amazing soundtrack aswell.\n\nI forgot to review it earlier, but now I feel like I have the obligation to recommend this to everyone.\n\n10/10. Best indie game I've ever played for sure.\n", "timestamp_created": 1584282853, "timestamp_updated": 1584282853, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 4, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.553605496883392334", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1383930480", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "65056106", "author": {"steamid": "76561198023814607", "personaname": "M4rt1nV", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/M4rt1nV/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 89, "pla